[Event "Knight School"]
[Opening "Queen's Pawn Game"]
[Variation "Stonewall Attack"]
[ECO "D00"]
[Character "solid,positional"]
[Risk "low"]
[EarlyMate "none"]
[Tricks "none"]
[Themes "bishop-out-first,attack-d4"]
[Kind "main"]

1. d4 d5 2. e3 Nf6 { Develops and covers e4 and d5, the squares White's pawns want. }
3. Bd3 ( 3. Nf3 e6 4. Bd3 c5 5. c3 Nc6 )
3... c5 { Strikes at d4 before White has a knight on f3 to defend it. White's bishop on d3 cannot do much against it. }
4. c3 ( 4. dxc5 e6 5. Nf3 Bxc5 6. O-O O-O )
( 4. Nf3 Nc6 5. c3 Bg4 )
4... Nc6 { A second attacker on d4, and a piece developed. }
5. f4 ( 5. Nf3 Bg4 { Pins the knight to the queen, so White cannot easily keep d4 defended. If h3, the bishop keeps the pin from h5. } 6. h3 Bh5 7. Nbd2 e6 )
5... Bg4 { Brings the c8 bishop out before ...e6 locks it in. It also pins nothing yet, but it stops a comfortable Nf3 and makes White spend a move on it. }
6. Nf3 ( 6. Be2 Bxe2 7. Qxe2 e6 8. Nf3 Bd6 )
( 6. Ne2 e6 7. O-O Bd6 8. Nd2 O-O )
6... e6 { Backs up d5 and opens the f8 bishop. The c8 bishop is already outside the pawn chain, which is the whole point of ...Bg4 first. }
7. Nbd2 Bd6 { Attacks the f4 pawn, which has no easy defender, and prepares to castle. }
8. O-O O-O { The king is safe before the f-file and the h-file open. }
9. Be2 cxd4 { Opens the c-file and trades off White's central pawn while the white pieces are not ready to recapture comfortably. }
10. cxd4 Rc8 { The rook takes the open file. White's e3 and f4 pawns have left the bishop on c1 boxed in, so Black's pieces are simply more active. } *
